          "Middle participles decline like first/second-declension adjectives. Masculine/neuter use second-declension endings, feminine uses the first-declension -η pattern. Their gender, number, and case agree with the person or thing described.",
          "Compare ὁ πορευόμενος στρατιώτης, subject singular, with τοὺς πορευομένους στρατιώτας, object plural. The ending tells you which noun the participle belongs to; it does not change who does the traveling.",
