    "translation": "Cyrus and the soldiers remain at Tarsus. The city is in Cilicia. The soldiers are unwilling to march; for they suspect a war against the Great King.\n\nSome of the soldiers say, “We are not serving against the King; we are not hired for this.” Clearchus first leads his own soldiers by force. They throw stones at him and the pack animals.\n\nForce does not help. Clearchus holds an assembly of his own soldiers and weeps. Those present are silent. He says, “You are my friends and allies; I remain with you.”\n\nThe listeners praise Clearchus. Many of the other soldiers come to him. Cyrus summons him; Clearchus does not come but secretly sends a messenger. He reports to Cyrus, “Take heart; matters are going well.”\n\nIn the assembly some seek the road home, while others speak about boats and guides. It is difficult to depart without Cyrus’s agreement. Supplies are in Cyrus’s market.\n\nThe soldiers send representatives to Cyrus. The representatives ask, “What do you want?” He says, “Abrocomas is my enemy; I want to march against him.” The representatives report the answer to the soldiers.\n\nThe soldiers still suspect the war against the King, but nevertheless decide to follow. They ask for greater pay, and Cyrus promises pay half as large again. Yet he does not openly state that he is leading them against the King.\n",
    "sourceCitation": "Xenophon, Anabasis 1.3.1–21. Controlled course adaptation; dialogue and teaching futures are newly supplied, not verbatim quotations. https://www.mikrosapoplous.gr/xenophon/anb3d10.htm https://beta.perseus.tufts.edu/urn%3Acts%3AgreekLit%3Atlg0032.tlg006.perseus-eng2%3A1.3/",
    "notesMarkdown": "Course adaptation of Xenophon, Anabasis 1.3.1–21. The refusal, violence against Clearchus, speeches, private message to Cyrus, negotiation, Abrocomas explanation, and increased pay follow the source. The short Greek speeches are newly written summaries, not quotations. The Great King remains a suspicion here: the public announcement comes at Thapsacus in Lesson 19."
  },
