    "introduction": [
      "At Cunaxa in 401 BCE, the Greek contingent wins against the troops directly facing it. Cyrus dies elsewhere on the field. The Greeks learn the decisive news only afterward; victory in one sector does not give Cyrus the throne.",
      "Source: Xenophon, Anabasis 1.8.17–29; 2.1.1–4. This is a controlled Attic Greek course adaptation, not a verbatim ancient extract. Sequence, persons, and historical outcomes follow the sources; sentence wording, compact transitions, and quoted speech are course compositions. Historical speakers are not being quoted verbatim.",
      "Aorist narrative is now a target. Blue glosses identify lexical irregularities and forms beyond this lesson: imperfects, passive or athematic aorists, perfect participles, and unfamiliar infinitives remain supported exposure rather than assessed production. Comparison passages from Memorabilia belong to a separate work and setting."
