        "prompt": "What status does the dream have?",
        "answer": "a reported dream with uncertain interpretation. The account preserves Xenophon’s fear as well as hope."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "What makes the replacement command collective?",
        "answer": "several officers deliberate and replacements are elected. The culture page identifies consultation and multiple elections."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "Who presses for prompt elections in the source?",
        "answer": "Cheirisophus. Cheirisophus contributes to the rebuilding of command."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "Does ignorance of danger suffice for courage in the comparison?",
        "answer": "no. Socrates distinguishes informed courage from ignorance."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "Why keep the works separate?",
        "answer": "to avoid inventing a camp reading of the later account. The comparison is editorial, not a fictional historical event."
      },
