          "prompt": "Which means “they released” (active)?",
          "answer": "ἔλυσαν. -σαν is third plural active in this pattern."
        },
        {
          "prompt": "Which means “we released” (middle)?",
          "answer": "ἐλυσάμεθα. -άμεθα marks first plural middle."
        },
        {
          "prompt": "What results from π + σ?",
          "answer": "ψ. A labial before σ combines as ψ."
        },
        {
          "prompt": "What results from χ + σ?",
          "answer": "ξ. A velar before σ combines as ξ."
        },
        {
          "prompt": "Which is first-aorist active nominative masculine singular?",
          "answer": "λύσας. λύσας is the unaugmented first-aorist active participle."
        },
        {
          "prompt": "Which is first-aorist middle nominative plural?",
          "answer": "λυσάμενοι. -άμενοι marks the first-aorist middle masculine plural."
        },
        {
          "prompt": "What do first and second aorists share?",
          "answer": "whole-action aorist aspect. The numbering labels formation, not a different aspect."
        },
        {
          "prompt": "Which is a thematic second aorist?",
          "answer": "ἔλαβον. λαβ- takes thematic ο/ε endings."
